Subject: Preserve original HBM UI requests under native compiler and pointer widths

Upstream-base: 132cdee912111da6c9973b1dce13651f1979b07d

Lower PPC fsel/fabs through their binary32 selection/sign contract and the
existing canonical OS fast-cast header. Keep original byte offsets full-width,
select canonical OS/GX owning declarations, and adapt the exact C++ allocation,
callback and switch syntax rejected by current compilers. Source algorithms,
request widths, choices and console bodies remain unchanged. No HBM admission,
raw resource/BE text readiness or physical speaker support follows this patch.

